course: dictionary
lesson: 140
title: An old tool called an adze
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An adze is an old cutting tool, a bit like an axe. The big difference is its blade: on an adze the blade is set across the handle, not in line with it. People use an adze to shape wood, taking off thin pieces bit by bit.
explain: Read the words around a new word for clues. «The canoe maker used an adze to shape the wood into a smooth boat.» Canoe, shape and wood tell you that an adze is a tool for working on wood. Ask yourself: what would fit here? A tool for wood.
explain: Sounds can help too. «"dzvinOk" means the bell, and the "dz" at its start is one sound, like in "adze".» Say adze slowly. The d and the z blend into one buzzing sound, the same sound you hear at the end of the word.
fact: An adze is a cutting tool with its blade set across the handle, while an axe has its blade in line with the handle.
fact: «Adze» means an old cutting tool used for shaping wood.
fact: Adzes have been used for a very long time, from the Stone Age to shipbuilding.
fact: Canoe makers in the Pacific, including Māori canoe makers, have used adzes to shape wood.
fact: In the US the word is also spelled «adz».
exercise: «The canoe maker used an adze to shape the wood.» What is an adze? | A kind of wild bird | A small boat for two people | *A cutting tool with its blade set across the handle | A musical instrument
exercise: How is an adze different from an axe? | *Its blade is set across the handle | It is made of paper | It has no blade at all | It is only used to play music
exercise: «The shipbuilder reached for her adze to shape the timber.» What is an adze mainly used for? | Painting pictures | *Shaping wood | Cooking soup | Catching fish
test: Which word means an old cutting tool with its blade across the handle? | hammock | castle | *adze | sail
test: In the US, how is this word also spelled? | *adz | adds | azd | adzze
exam: «The shipbuilder used an adze to shape the timber, and its blade sat across the handle.» What is the main job of an adze in this sentence? | Lighting a fire | Carrying people across the sea | *Shaping wood | Pumping water
